      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think .useVndk() just tells us if the built module is for vendor or product partition. it\u0027s more like \"module is ABLE to use vndk, if there is any vndk\". so we need to guard some of these logics with IsVndkDeprecated() to accomdate for builds with and without VNDK during this transition period",
